    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and it passes. The full build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` field on owners, returned as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nTwo changes, each in the layer where it belongs:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` (read-only string) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in every owner response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 computed the value during the existing `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` mapping via a MapStruct expression backed by a small `formatDisplayName(owner)` helper (`lastName + \", \" + firstName`). This keeps the presentation formatting in the mapper (DTO shaping) rather than polluting the `Owner` domain entity, and applies uniformly to create, get, list, and page responses since they all go through `toOwnerDto`.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
